      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Acids"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Acids produce hydrogen ions (H+) in aqueous solution and turn blue litmus red.",
        "Bases produce hydroxide ions (OH-) in aqueous solution, feel soapy to touch, and turn red litmus blue.",
        "Alkalis are water-soluble bases such as Sodium Hydroxide (NaOH) and Potassium Hydroxide (KOH).",
        "The pH scale measures the hydrogen ion concentration; values less than 7 represent acidic solutions, while values greater than 7 represent basic solutions.",
        "Neutralization is the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water, accompanied by evolution of heat."
      ],
      "id": "lmg7t0y"
    },
